You're a sick little monkey.

>...

>3) The T-1000, HP N/A, HD 10, immune to all attacks from physical weapons.
>There is only one method to kill a T-1000. First, hit it with a wand of
>cold until it freezes. Second, hit it with a wand of Magic Missile to
>shatter it. and Finally, zap it with a wand of fire to melt it forever.

No, that's ridiculous.

Have weapons affect it normally.  Perhaps Frost Brand could do extra
damage, and a cold-based spell could immobilize it for awhile, or
maybe even make it easier to kill.  A blast of fire might stun it for
a while (as the direct hit with the grenade launcher).  You shouldn't
need some ridiculous arsenal of wands to kill it.

HOWEVER, it should regnerate at a pretty good clip, say 10->15
HP/round.  In addition, it shouldn't stay dead.  After you destroy it,
it just comes back again in a few turns, like a troll, and it always
leaves a corpse (a seething silver puddle).

Getting rid of the corpse should be a big problem.  If you eat it, you
get mercury poisoning (sickness) and die shortly unless cured.  Polymorph
shouldn't affect the corpse.  Perhaps reading a tower of flame scroll
in the near vicinity of the corpse will take it out.  That scroll
isn't otherwise good for much, and exacts a price for the benefit of
wiping out the T-1000 for good.

The best bet is just to kill it once and get the hell off the level.
Of course, it's waiting for you on the way back up.  Make it fast (like
some of the insects) so if you just run it will probably be next to you
on the stairs and follow you to the next level.  You need to kill it
at least once.

Speaking of polymorph, let it polymorph so that it looks like a
random ordinary humanoid...until it attacks.  Then, you'll know that
it's a T-1000 hill orc (or hobbit, or elf).  Zapping it with a polymorph
wand will cause it to change its appearance randomly, but it will retain
the same statistics and abilities (and keep attacking).

This one should pick up and use weapons but not armor.  It should get
two attacks per round.  It should be capable of throwing as other
humanoids are.

It should ooze under locked doors.

With their advanced infrared capabilities, all terminators should detect
invisible.

